lowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T13:39:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T13:40:52Z","body":"> The implementation overall looks fine (aside from the String/StringName inconsistency), however as mentioned in the linked discussion, there might be a better way to implement this. Like, why is it specifically in Control nodes, while localization is a feature of Node (see `auto_translation`)? I imagine the property is also relevant for e.g. Label3D.\r\n\r\nI've been thinking about this, I pretty much agree with you there, shouldn't be a `Control` exclusive and it should be just an extra type check in `packed_scene_translation_parser_plugin.cpp` for `Label3D`, but there're a couple problems:\r\n\r\n- Even though `Label3D` should theoretically have translations, it doesn't have the same `localize_numeral_system` property, and along with it the Localization group, so apparently label 3d is its own thing.\r\n- Should I move `translation_context` property to `Node`, would it go inside the `auto_translate` group under Node? I'd say translation context is also its own thing, ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796679262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.gi